A literal infinite perpetual-motion money machine doesn’t exist. Every real business eventually encounters competition, costs, regulation, or changing demand.

What you can build are systems that compound and become increasingly self-sustaining. Think of them as flywheels instead of perpetual-motion machines.

Here are several “money engines” that reinforce one another:

1. The Knowledge Flywheel

Research
    ↓
Distill into operators
    ↓
Open-source examples
    ↓
Community trust
    ↓
Consulting / Enterprise
    ↓
Revenue
    ↓
More research

2. The Software Flywheel

Free Tool
    ↓
Users
    ↓
Feedback
    ↓
Better Product
    ↓
Paid Version
    ↓
Recurring Revenue
    ↓
Faster Development

3. The AI Agent Factory

Build one excellent AI workflow.

That workflow builds the next workflow.

Eventually you have specialized agents for:

* sales
* marketing
* coding
* documentation
* customer support
* research

Each reduces labor needed to create the next product.

