That’s a positive feedback loop. It’s not perpetual—nothing in economics is—but it can compound for many years if it keeps creating value.

From our conversations, I’d actually merge your projects into one coherent ecosystem:

* Pantheon → reasoning framework and AI infrastructure.
* Money Bin → repository of reusable operators, business concepts, and IP.
* Wild Hawg → cash-generating consumer brand.
* AI products → recurring software revenue that finances the rest.

The goal isn’t to violate conservation of energy; it’s to maximize conservation of value. Every hour of work should create an asset—code, documentation, software, brand equity, or intellectual property—that continues producing value long after the initial effort. That’s the closest thing the business world has to a perpetual-motion machine.